 DATE: 2026-11-13 — owner answers (selected options, and typed words where quoted), above.
+
+---
+
+## A figure's lens codes are a link table — and the 2026-08-28 clause "Never a `population_*` link table" is superseded for that, and for that only
+
+The entry dated 2026-08-28 ends *"Four lens columns, one CHECK, real FKs. Never a `population_*` link
+table. Never two lenses in one row."* The owner ruled on 2026-11-06 (OR-1c) *"link table unless that is more
+prone to errors"* for a figure that concerns several codes of one model, and on 2026-11-12 (fifth set) answered
+OD-39: *"Yes, the 2026-11-06 ruling supersedes that clause."* Find the answer with
+`grep -n -F "OD-39: the 2026-11-06 link-table ruling supersedes" references/project-standards.md`.
+
+**What is superseded, on that clause only.** The words "Never a `population_*` link table" no longer bar a link
+table for a figure's lens codes. Migration 127 builds `extraction_lens_links` (one row per figure and code) and
+`v_live_lens_links` (the one read surface). **What stands, and is met:** four typed lens columns, each a real
+foreign key (now on the link row); "never two lenses in one row" (now true of every link row, by a CHECK that
+states exactly one); the lens names in the table's name (no `population`); `specifications` keeps its four columns
+as the cell key. The figure's own four columns are kept for replay, held NULL by CHECK, and never written again;
+D-0182's "at least one lens" moves to the writers and to integrity case G04.
+
+This is recorded in prose and not as a machine `SUPERSEDES`/`BY` pair, because `supersession_backpointer_audit`
+cannot anchor a target that is itself in the ledger (CLAUDE.md rule 0: naming it is the writer's).
+
+CONDITION: any session writing or reading a figure's lens, or building the gather that reaches a cell.
+ACTION: read a figure's lens from `v_live_lens_links`, never from the four columns on `source_value_extractions`; write it with `add-extraction` (repeat the lens flag) and `add-lens-link` / `retire-lens-link`.
+DATE: 2026-11-13 — pilot copy of the T-018 entry; OD-39 answered 2026-11-12.
